  "about": "The application comparisons (C1, N2; lead design §2a.1), run by `omui-devtools bench apps`: every side built at its pin, launched in an 800 × 600 window of an X server the harness starts (1920 × 1080, no window manager), measured from outside its process — start to the first presented frame equal to the settled picture (cold: its files dropped from the page cache; warm: at once again), memory at rest (pmap: private dirty, USS, PSS, RSS) `rest_ms` after that frame, the processor (mcpplibs.os), context switches (pidstat) and frames drawn over `idle_ms` at rest, and `clicks` clicks (XTEST) from letting go to the first frame that changes `label`. A side in `motion` is measured over the same span while it moves — `live` by itself (the market board: omui's tests/bench core/live-dashboard, NSH's Stocks), `scroll` with the wheel turned every 1/120 s (10,000 rows): the frames presented a second, the interval between them (p50, p95, p99), the processor per frame. `click` is the button's centre in the window, `label` the part of it the click changes (x, y, width, height). Their builds use the system's compilers; NSH's as its report builds its hello worlds (LTO fat, one unit, stripped), Slint's the same (slint/Cargo.toml).",
